# Line-ending policy.
#
# Why this file exists: this project ships Windows batch launchers. A .bat
# file with LF-only line endings can break under cmd.exe -- `goto :label`
# and multi-line if blocks are the first things to misbehave -- and the
# symptom is confusing because the file looks perfectly fine in an editor.
#
# `eol=crlf` makes git store LF internally (clean diffs, works on any
# platform) but always check CRLF out into the working tree, regardless of
# what the user's core.autocrlf is set to. Without this, anyone who clones
# with autocrlf=false silently receives launchers that do not run.
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.vbs   text eol=crlf

# Never apply any text transformation to binaries: a stray CR byte
# corrupts them.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.icns  binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip   binary
*.exe   binary
